{"format":2,"id":"spanish","name":"Spanish","icon":"💃","color":"#F59E0B","category":"language","subcategory":"spanish","tags":["voice","beginner"],"version":1,"description":"Everyday Spanish words, handy phrases and short sentences.","question":"What does “{prompt}” mean?","reverseQuestion":"How do you say “{answer}” in Spanish?","typeable":true,"skillNoun":"Lengua","lang":"es-ES","cards":[{"id":"hola","prompt":"hola","answer":"hello","alts":["hi"],"options":["goodbye","please","thank you"],"fact":"The \"h\" in hola is silent: say \"OH-la.\"","difficulty":1},{"id":"adios","prompt":"adiós","answer":"goodbye","alts":["bye"],"options":["hello","good night","see you"],"fact":"Adiós comes from \"a Dios,\" meaning \"to God.\"","difficulty":1},{"id":"gracias","prompt":"gracias","answer":"thank you","alts":["thanks"],"options":["please","sorry","excuse me"],"fact":"Add \"muchas\" for \"muchas gracias,\" thank you very much.","difficulty":1},{"id":"por-favor","prompt":"por favor","answer":"please","options":["thank you","excuse me","you're welcome"],"fact":"Por favor literally means \"for favor.\"","difficulty":1},{"id":"buenos-dias","prompt":"buenos días","answer":"good morning","alts":["good day"],"options":["good night","good afternoon","goodbye"],"fact":"Spanish greetings are plural: literally \"good days.\"","difficulty":1},{"id":"buenas-noches","prompt":"buenas noches","answer":"good night","alts":["good evening"],"options":["good morning","good afternoon","see you later"],"fact":"Buenas noches works both as an evening hello and as goodnight.","difficulty":1},{"id":"si","prompt":"sí","answer":"yes","options":["no","if","maybe"],"fact":"The accent matters: sí means \"yes,\" but si without it means \"if.\"","difficulty":1},{"id":"el-perro","prompt":"el perro","answer":"dog","alts":["the dog"],"options":["cat","horse","bird"],"fact":"In some countries a hot dog is called a \"perro caliente.\"","difficulty":1},{"id":"el-gato","prompt":"el gato","answer":"cat","alts":["the 