erican Southwest.","difficulty":1},{"id":"rojo","prompt":"rojo","answer":"red","options":["blue","yellow","green"],"fact":"Colors usually follow the noun: \"el coche rojo\" is \"the red car.\"","difficulty":1},{"id":"azul","prompt":"azul","answer":"blue","options":["green","gray","purple"],"fact":"Azul doesn't change with gender: el mar azul, la casa azul.","difficulty":1},{"id":"verde","prompt":"verde","answer":"green","options":["red","brown","blue"],"fact":"\"Verde que te quiero verde\" opens a famous poem by Federico García Lorca.","difficulty":1},{"id":"la-madre","prompt":"la madre","answer":"mother","alts":["the mother","mom","mum"],"options":["father","sister","grandmother"],"fact":"Most people say \"mamá\" at home; \"madre\" is more formal.","difficulty":1},{"id":"el-hermano","prompt":"el hermano","answer":"brother","alts":["the brother"],"options":["sister","cousin","uncle"],"fact":"The plural \"hermanos\" can mean brothers or siblings in general.","difficulty":1},{"id":"la-playa","prompt":"la playa","answer":"beach","alts":["the beach"],"options":["sea","mountain","river"],"fact":"Spain's Mediterranean coast is famous for its playas, like the Costa del Sol.","difficulty":1},{"id":"el-queso","prompt":"el queso","answer":"cheese","alts":["the cheese"],"options":["bread","butter","ham"],"fact":"The quesadilla gets its name from queso.","difficulty":1},{"id":"comer","prompt":"comer","answer":"to eat","alts":["eat"],"options":["to drink","to cook","to sleep"],"fact":"\"Comida\" means food, and in Spain also the big midday meal.","difficulty":2},{"id":"beber","prompt":"beber","answer":"to drink","alts":["drink"],"options":["to eat","to swim","to wash"],"fact":"For drinks, many speakers say \"tomar\" instead: \"¿Qué vas a tomar?\"","difficulty":2},{"id":"dormir","prompt":"dormir","answer":"to sleep","alts":["sleep"],"options":["to dream","to rest","to wake up"],"fact":"A \"dormitorio\" is a bedroom, from the same root.","difficulty":2},{"id":"hablar","prompt":"hablar","answer":"to speak","alts":["speak","to talk","talk"],"options":["to listen","to sing","to write"],"fact":"\"¿Hablas inglés?\" asks a friend if they speak English.","difficulty":2},{"id":"correr","prompt":"correr","answer":"to run","alts":["run"],"options":["to walk","to jump","to swim"],"fact":"A runner is a \"corredor.\"","difficulty":2},{"id":"escribir","prompt":"escribir","answer":"to write","alts":["write"],"options":["to read","to draw","to speak"],"fact":"A writer is an \"escritor,\" and a desk is an \"escritorio.\"","difficulty":2},{"id":"leer","prompt":"leer","answer":"to read","alts":["read"],"options":["to write","to learn","to look"],"fact":"A reader is a \"lector.\"","difficulty":2},{"id":"aprender","prompt":"aprender","answer":"to learn","alts":["learn"],"options":["to teach","to read","to forget"],"fact":"An apprentice is an \"aprendiz,\" from the same root.","difficulty":2},{"id":"grande","prompt":"grande","answer":"big","alts":["large"],"options":["small","tall","long"],"fact":"Before a singular noun it shortens to \"gran\": \"un gran día,\" a great day.","difficulty":2},{"id":"pequeno","prompt":"pequeño","answer":"small","alts":["little"],"options":["big","short","thin"],"fact":"Add a diminutive for extra cuteness: \"pequeñito,\" teeny.","difficulty":2},{"id":"feliz","prompt":"feliz","answer":"happy","alts":["glad"],"options":["sad","tired","angry"],"fact":"\"¡Feliz cumpleaños!\" means \"Happy birthday!\"","difficulty":2},{"id":"cansado","prompt":"cansado","answer":"tired","alts":["weary"],"options":["bored","sick","hungry"],"fact":"A woman would say \"estoy cansada,\" with an -a ending.","difficulty":2},{"id":"rapido","prompt":"rápido","answer":"fast","alts":["quick","rapid"],"options":["slow","strong","early"],"fact":"Add -mente for the adverb: \"rápidamente,\" quickly.","difficulty":2},{"id":"caliente","prompt":"caliente","answer":"hot","alts":["warm"],"options":["cold","wet","spicy"],"fact":"For weather, say \"hace calor,\" not \"caliente.\"","difficulty":2},{"id":"frio","prompt":"frío","answer":"cold","options":["hot","dry","windy"],"fact":"\"Hace frío\" means \"it's cold\" when talking about weather.","difficulty":2},{"id":"hoy","prompt":"hoy","answer":"today","options":["tomorrow","yesterday","tonight"],"fact":"\"Hoy en día\" means \"nowadays.\"","difficulty":2},{"id":"manana","prompt":"mañana","answer":"tomorrow","alts":["morning"],"options":["today","yesterday","tonight"],"fact":"Mañana also means morning, so \"mañana por la mañana\" is tomorrow morning.","difficulty":2},{"id":"ayer","prompt":"ayer","answer":"yesterday","options":["today","tomorrow","later"],"fact":"The day before yesterday is \"anteayer.\"","difficulty":2},{"id":"siempre","prompt":"siempre","answer":"always","alts":["forever"],"options":["never","sometimes","often"],"fact":"Its opposite is \"nunca,\" never.","difficulty":2},{"id":"como-estas","prompt":"¿Cómo estás?","answer":"How are you?","options":["Where are you?","Who are you?","How old are you?"],"fact":"Use \"¿Cómo está usted?\" to ask someone politely or formally.","difficulty":2},{"id":"mucho-gusto","prompt":"mucho gusto","answer":"nice to meet you","alts":["pleased to meet you"],"options":["see you soon","good luck","very good"],"fact":"Mucho gusto literally means \"much pleasure.\"","difficulty":2},{"id":"lo-siento","prompt":"lo siento","answer":"I'm sorry","alts":["sorry","I am sorry"],"options":["excuse me","I feel fine","no problem"],"fact":"Lo siento literally means \"I feel it.\"","difficulty":2},{"id":"de-nada","prompt":"de nada","answer":"you're welcome","alts":["you are welcome","no problem"],"options":["nothing new","thank you","never mind"],"fact":"De nada literally means \"of nothing,\" the usual reply to \"gracias.\"","difficulty":2},{"id":"cuanto-cuesta","prompt":"¿Cuánto cuesta?","answer":"How much does it cost?","alts":["How much is it?","How much?"],"options":["What time is it?","Where is it?","How many are there?"],"fact":"For more than one item, ask \"¿Cuánto cuestan?\"","difficulty":2},{"id":"tengo-hambre","prompt":"tengo hambre","answer":"I'm hungry","alts":["I am hungry"],"options":["I'm thirsty","I'm tired","I'm cold"],"fact":"Spanish says \"I have hunger,\" not \"I am hungry.\"","difficulty":2},{"id":"buena-suerte","prompt":"buena suerte","answer":"good luck","options":["good night","good job","have fun"],"fact":"Friends also say \"¡Mucha suerte!\" for lots of luck.","difficulty":2},{"id":"donde-esta-la-biblioteca","prompt":"¿Dónde está la biblioteca?","answer":"Where is the library?","alts":["Where's the library?"],"options":["Where is the bookstore?","When does the library open?","Is the library big?"],"fact":"Spanish questions open with an upside-down ¿ so you know a question is coming.","difficulty":3},{"id":"no-hablo-espanol","prompt":"No hablo español.","answer":"I don't speak Spanish.","alts":["I do not speak Spanish"],"options":["I speak a little Spanish.","I don't understand Spanish.","He doesn't speak Spanish."],"fact":"Spanish puts \"no\" right before the verb to make it negative.","difficulty":3},{"id":"habla-usted-ingles","prompt":"¿Habla usted inglés?","answer":"Do you speak English?","options":["Do you understand English?","Are you English?","Do you study English?"],"fact":"\"Usted\" is the polite \"you,\" handy with strangers.","difficulty":3},{"id":"me-gustaria-un-cafe","prompt":"Me gustaría un café, por favor.","answer":"I would like a coffee, please.","alts":["I'd like a coffee, please","I would like a coffee","I'd like a coffee"],"options":["I like coffee a lot.","Do you have coffee, please?","I would like a tea, please."],"fact":"\"Me gustaría\" is a polite way to ask for something, like \"I would like.\"","difficulty":3},{"id":"la-cuenta-por-favor","prompt":"La cuenta, por favor.","answer":"The check, please.","alts":["The bill, please","The check please","The bill please"],"options":["The menu, please.","The table, please.","The story, please."],"fact":"In Spain waiters rarely bring the bill until you ask for it.","difficulty":3},{"id":"puede-ayudarme","prompt":"¿Puede ayudarme?","answer":"Can you help me?","alts":["Could you help me?"],"options":["Can I help you?","Can you call me?","Do you need help?"],"fact":"Pronouns can attach to the end of an infinitive: ayudar + me = ayudarme.","difficulty":3},{"id":"estoy-perdido","prompt":"Estoy perdido.","answer":"I'm lost.","alts":["I am lost"],"options":["I'm tired.","I'm late.","I'm sick."],"fact":"A woman would say \"Estoy perdida.\"","difficulty":3},{"id":"hace-buen-tiempo-hoy","prompt":"Hace buen tiempo hoy.","answer":"The weather is nice today.","alts":["It's nice weather today","It is nice weather today","The weather is good today","Nice weather today"],"options":["It is raining today.","I have time today.","It is very cold today."],"fact":"\"Tiempo\" means both weather and time.","difficulty":3},{"id":"mi-hermana-es-medica","prompt":"Mi hermana es médica.","answer":"My sister is a doctor.","options":["My brother is a doctor.","My sister is sick.","My sister is a teacher."],"fact":"Spanish drops the article before professions: no \"una\" needed.","difficulty":3},{"id":"el-tren-sale-a-las-ocho","prompt":"El tren sale a las ocho.","answer":"The train leaves at eight.","alts":["The train leaves at eight o'clock","The train leaves at 8"],"options":["The train arrives at eight.","The bus leaves at eight.","The train has eight cars."],"fact":"Clock times use \"a las\": \"a las ocho,\" at eight.","difficulty":3},{"id":"quiero-aprender-espanol","prompt":"Quiero aprender español.","answer":"I want to learn Spanish.","options":["I already speak Spanish.","I want to teach Spanish.","I love Spanish food."],"fact":"\"Querer\" plus an infinitive means \"to want to do\" something.","difficulty":3},{"id":"no-entiendo","prompt":"No entiendo.","answer":"I don't understand.","alts":["I do not understand"],"options":["I don't know.","I can't hear.","I don't agree."],"fact":"Pair it with \"¿Puede repetir?\" (Can you repeat?) and you can survive any conversation.","difficulty":3},{"id":"que-significa-esta-palabra","prompt":"¿Qué significa esta palabra?","answer":"What does this word mean?","options":["How do you spell this word?","Is this word Spanish?","What is your name?"],"fact":"Significar means \"to mean,\" cousin of the English \"signify.\"","difficulty":3},{"id":"a-que-hora-abre-el-museo","prompt":"¿A qué hora abre el museo?","answer":"What time does the museum open?","alts":["When does the museum open?"],"options":["What time does the museum close?","Where is the museum?","How much is the museum?"],"fact":"Madrid's Prado Museum offers free entry during its last opening hours most days.","difficulty":3},{"id":"me-duele-la-cabeza","prompt":"Me duele la cabeza.","answer":"My head hurts.","alts":["I have a headache"],"options":["My stomach hurts.","I hit my head.","My back hurts."],"fact":"Spanish says \"the head hurts me,\" just like \"me gusta\" means \"it pleases me.\"","difficulty":3},{"id":"necesito-un-medico","prompt":"Necesito un médico.","answer":"I need a doctor.","options":["I am a doctor.","I need medicine.","I need a hospital."],"fact":"In an emergency in Spain, dial 112.","difficulty":3},{"id":"hace-calor-en-verano","prompt":"Hace calor en verano.","answer":"It's hot in summer.","alts":["It is hot in summer","It's hot in the summer","It is hot in the summer"],"options":["It's cold in winter.","It's warm in spring.","It's hot today."],"fact":"Spanish uses \"hacer\" (to make) for weather: \"hace calor,\" \"hace sol.\"","difficulty":3},{"id":"tengo-dos-gatos","prompt":"Tengo dos gatos.","answer":"I have two cats.","options":["I have two dogs.","I have three cats.","I want two cats."],"fact":"Most Spanish nouns ending in a vowel form plurals by adding -s: gato → gatos.","difficulty":3}]}